# Production release-control ownership. This single owner routes review but is
# not separation of duties. These rules become enforcement only when the
# main-branch ruleset requires an independent Code Owner review, prevents
# self-approval, and the Production environment uses a separate required
# approver and restricted secret administrator. The deployment runbook requires
# operators to verify those external settings before clearance. This file still
# has one owner, so a second independently controlled owner or team must be added
# before that owner can author a releasable control change; the release verifier
# intentionally requires the live Code Owner-review rule and otherwise blocks.
